":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haitian_Revolution","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"The revolution overthrew French colonial rule in Saint-Domingue and produced independent Haiti.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04479","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4480","nodeId":"REVISION85-4480","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Mexican Revolution began against the long rule of:","value":"Porfirio Díaz","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexican_Revolution","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Opposition to Díaz helped trigger the revolution of 1910.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04480","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4481","nodeId":"REVISION85-4481","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Suez Crisis followed the nationalisation of the canal by:","value":"Egypt","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suez_Crisis","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Egypt's president Gamal Abdel Nasser nationalised the canal company in 1956.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04481","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4482","nodeId":"REVISION85-4482","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The term decolonisation refers to:","value":"The end of colonial rule","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decolonization","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Decolonisation involves colonies gaining independence or otherwise ending colonial subordination.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04482","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4483","nodeId":"REVISION85-4483","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Spanish Republic faced a military rebellion led ultimately by:","value":"Francisco Franco","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish_Civil_War","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Franco emerged as leader of the Nationalist side during the Spanish Civil War.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04483","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4484","nodeId":"REVISION85-4484","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Warsaw Pact was a:","value":"Soviet-led military alliance","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warsaw_Pact","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"The Warsaw Pact linked the Soviet Union with allied Eastern European states.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04484","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4485","nodeId":"REVISION85-4485","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Prague Spring was ended by an invasion led by the:","value":"Soviet Union","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prague_Spring","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Warsaw Pact forces led by the Soviet Union suppressed Czechoslovakia's reform movement in 1968.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04485","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4486","nodeId":"REVISI